{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2086,2148p' test/yang/clojure_test.clj && sed -n '151,202p' test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj && sed -n '300,340p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(deftest test-common-call-cell-ref-map-invocation\n  (testing \"a full-shape data map with a 64-character seal is ordinary invocable data\"\n    ;; The map spells every key of an issued reference and the seal has the\n    ;; issued format; its :id names nothing in the engine's heap id language\n    ;; (:cell-N), so it can never be genuine and its invocation is the map\n    ;; lookup, on both evaluators, where the previous rounds' shape gates\n    ;; routed it to admission and the dereference refused it.\n    (is (= [:yin.k/ok :cell-ref]\n           (run-library '[(let [m {:type :cell-ref :id :some-key :seal \"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"}]\n                            (m :type))])))\n    (is (= [:yin.k/ok :some-key]\n           (run-library '[(let [m {:type :cell-ref :id :some-key :seal \"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"}]\n                            (m :id))]))))\n  (testing \"a runtime-built full-shape map (assoc, not a bound literal) invokes as data\"\n    (is (= [:yin.k/ok :cell-ref]\n           (run-library '[(let [m (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :type :cell-ref)\n                                                :id :some-key)\n                                         :seal \"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\")]\n                            (m :type))]))))\n  (testing \"a full-shape map that is data is not call-eligible\"\n    (is (= [:yin.k/ok false]\n           (run-library '[(yang.call/eligible? {:type :cell-ref :id :some-key\n                                                :seal \"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"})]))))\n  (testing \"genuine references still dereference through admission\"\n    ;; A cell the engine minted (:cell-0), holding a descriptor with a\n    ;; callable entry: the call reaches the entry.\n    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok :called]\n             (run-cell-probe (u/app (u/v 'cell/new)\n                                    (u/app (u/v 'assoc) (u/lit {})\n                                           (u/lit :yang.call/entry)\n                                           (u/lam ['invocation] (u/lit :called))))\n                             lane))\n          (str lane \" genuine live\"))))\n  (testing \"a genuine-but-dead reference keeps the standing refusal\"\n    ;; A genuine cell whose contents carry no call entry: admission answers\n    ;; false and the call refuses as not-callable — the behavior the D2 bar\n    ;; pins, unchanged by the data fallback.\n    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\n      (let [[tag payload :as result] (run-cell-probe (u/app (u/v 'cell/new) (u/lit 42))\n                                                     lane)]\n        (is (and (= :yin.k/error tag)\n                 (= :yang.call/not-callable (:yang.call/reason payload)))\n            (str lane \" genuine dead: \" (pr-str result))))))\n  (testing \"the residual, pinned: a forged id inside the heap language fails closed in the VM\"\n    ;; A map whose :id is a :cell-N keyword and whose seal has the issued\n    ;; format but not the issued content: it is a dereference candidate the\n    ;; VM's heap+seal check rejects — a host-level refusal, the same fate\n    ;; any forged reference meets anywhere in the system. No in-language\n    ;; authenticity probe exists (check-ref! throws past every guest catch),\n    ;; so this class stays fail-closed until yin.vm publishes one.\n    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\n      (is (= [:thrown {:reason :dead-or-forged-reference, :effect :cell/get}]\n             (run-cell-probe (u/lit {:type :cell-ref :id :cell-7\n                                     :seal \"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"})\n                             lane))\n          (str lane \" forged in-language id\")))))\n\n\n(deftest test-library-closes-over-its-own-names\n  (testing \"library-for returns the definitions a program mentions, transitively\"\n    (let [names (set (map second (yang/library-for '[(seq? x)])))]\n      (is (every? names '[seq? sequential? vector? map? set? coll?])\n(deftest clojure-source-cell-ref-map-invocation-test\n  (testing \"a source map {:type :cell-ref} is ordinary invocable data\"\n    ;; The donor's exported function invokes its own source map literal:\n    ;; the map lookup answers 42, where the structural cell test used to\n    ;; dereference the map as a cell and fail the VM.\n    (is (= {:js/out [\"42n\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n           (xl/call [:clojure\n                     \"(defn probe [] ({:type :cell-ref :marker 42} :marker))\"]\n                    [\"probe\"]\n                    [:typescript \"console.log(probe());\"]))))\n  (testing \"a source map with the full forged cell-ref shape is ordinary invocable data\"\n    ;; The map spells every key of an issued reference among its own\n    ;; entries; it is still data, so the lookup answers 42 where key\n    ;; presence alone used to dereference it and fail the VM.\n    (is (= {:js/out [\"42n\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n           (xl/call [:clojure\n                     \"(defn probe [] ({:type :cell-ref :id :customer :seal \\\"wax\\\" :marker 42} :marker))\"]\n                    [\"probe\"]\n                    [:typescript \"console.log(probe());\"]))))\n  (testing \"a full-shape three-entry map with a valid-format 64-char seal is ordinary invocable data\"\n    ;; The exact issued format — three entries, a seal string of the issued\n    ;; length — with an :id the engine's heap could never have minted (heap\n    ;; ids are :cell-N keywords): the map can never be a reference, so the\n    ;; invocation is the map lookup and answers the stored seal string,\n    ;; where the shape gates of the previous rounds routed it to admission\n    ;; and the dereference refused the VM.\n    (is (= {:js/out [(str \"\\\"\" (apply str (repeat 64 \"a\")) \"\\\"\")], :js/uncaught nil}\n           (xl/call [:clojure\n                     (str \"(defn probe [] ({:type :cell-ref :id :some-key \"\n                          \":seal \\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\"} :seal))\")]\n                    [\"probe\"]\n                    [:typescript \"console.log(probe());\"]))))\n  (testing \"a runtime-built full-shape map (assoc-constructed, not a bound literal) invokes as data\"\n    ;; The map is assembled by assoc at runtime, so no literal ever holds\n    ;; it; the shape test runs on the constructed value and the lookup\n    ;; still answers the stored seal string.\n    (is (= {:js/out [(str \"\\\"\" (apply str (repeat 64 \"a\")) \"\\\"\")], :js/uncaught nil}\n           (xl/call [:clojure\n                     (str \"(defn probe [] (let [m (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :type :cell-ref) \"\n                          \":id :some-key) \"\n                          \":seal \\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\")] \"\n                          \"(m :seal)))\")]\n                    [\"probe\"]\n                    [:typescript \"console.log(probe());\"]))))\n  (testing \"a runtime-built map with the forged cell-ref shape is ordinary invocable data\"\n    (is (= {:js/out [\"42n\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n           (xl/call [:clojure\n                     \"(defn probe [] (let [m {:type :cell-ref :id :customer :seal \\\"wax\\\" :marker 42}] (m :marker)))\"]\n                    [\"probe\"]\n                    [:typescript \"console.log(probe());\"])))))\n\n\n  \"The seal of a `kind` reference to resource `id` under `secret`.\"\n  [secret kind id]\n  (jing/content-hash [:yin.k/seal secret kind id] {:algorithm :blake3}))\n\n\n(defn- cursor-cell?\n  \"True when a resource is a cursor cell, `{:stream-id id :cursor c}`.\n   A cursor cell is the VM's mutable box (with identity) holding one\n   immutable `dao.stream` cursor; `:stream/next` overwrites its `:cursor`\n   with the successor. A guest program holds a sealed `:cursor-ref` naming\n   it, never the cell itself. Not to be confused with `yin.vm.cell`, the\n   general heap box. Vocabulary: UCF §7.5.3, \\\"Terminology\\\".\"\n  [resource]\n  (and (map? resource) (contains? resource :stream-id)))\n\n\n(defn issue-ref\n  \"A reference of `kind` (`:stream-ref`, `:cursor-ref`, or `:cell-ref`) to\n   resource or heap cell `id`, sealed under the task's capability secret.\n   A task composed\n   without a secret cannot issue one: it fails closed rather than issue a\n   reference anyone could forge.\"\n  [state kind id]\n  (let [secret (:capability-secret state)]\n    (when (nil? secret)\n      (fail (str \"This task has no capability secret, so it cannot issue\"\n                 \" a resource reference\")\n            {:reason :no-capability-secret, :kind kind, :id id}))\n    {:type kind, :id id, :seal (seal-of secret kind id)}))\n\n\n(defn authentic-ref?\n  \"True when `ref` is a `kind` reference this task issued: its seal\n   verifies under the task's secret, and it names a live resource of that\n   kind. A `:cell-ref` is checked against `:heap` instead: its id is live\n   by `contains?` (a cell may hold nil) and its seal equals the one the\n   heap entry recorded at allocation, so no hash is computed per access.\"\n  [state kind ref]\n  (let [secret (:capability-secret state)\n        id (when (map? ref) (:id ref))]\n    (if (= :cell-ref kind)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
