{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794300000000-reviewer-cljrt-r3.codex.stdout.log\\\"; [print(x[\\\"item\\\"][\\\"text\\\"]) for l in open(p) if (x:=json.loads(l)).get(\\\"item\\\",{}).get(\\\"type\\\")==\\\"agent_message\\\"]' \"","aggregated_output":"python3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-B1arktF7' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-04 17:55:00.550 xcodebuild[27137:109273886]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-04 17:55:00.873 xcodebuild[27137:109273884] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\npython3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-Z6Zp1hjA' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-04 17:55:01.521 xcodebuild[27143:109273926]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-04 17:55:01.751 xcodebuild[27143:109273924] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <listcomp>\n  File \"/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Library/Frameworks/Python3.framework/Versions/3.9/lib/python3.9/json/__init__.py\", line 346, in loads\n    return _default_decoder.decode(s)\n  File \"/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Library/Frameworks/Python3.framework/Versions/3.9/lib/python3.9/json/decoder.py\", line 337, in decode\n    obj, end = self.raw_decode(s, idx=_w(s, 0).end())\n  File \"/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Library/Frameworks/Python3.framework/Versions/3.9/lib/python3.9/json/decoder.py\", line 355, in raw_decode\n    raise JSONDecodeError(\"Expecting value\", s, err.value) from None\njson.decoder.JSONDecodeError: Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)\nI’ll review the round 3 diff and the relevant runtime admission paths statically, including the unchanged D2 and round 2 boundaries. I won’t run test suites.\nThe new gate still recognizes references by their public map shape. I’m tracing the resulting failure path and the VM’s actual reference representation to determine whether a format-matching ordinary map remains a counterexample.\n**REJECT for landing.** The round 3 gate still treats an ordinary source map as a cell reference based on its public shape.\n\nAt [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1224), a three-entry map with `:type :cell-ref`, `:id`, and any 64-character string for `:seal` passes the structural test. For example, invoking such a map with `:id` should return its stored value, but the routing at [line 1343](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1343) sends it to admission, which calls `cell/get` at [line 2184](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2184). The VM rejects the invalid seal or nonexistent cell instead of performing the map lookup. The seal prevents a capability bypass; it does not establish ordinary map semantics.\n\nGenuine issued references have the tested shape and continue through admission to the common invoker when their cell contains a callable entry. But the claimed distinction between genuine and non-genuine references is not made by the shape check: [the VM issues references as maps](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:316), and authenticity is established separately against the heap and seal.\n\nThe new tests at [cross_lang_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj:161) concretely assert `42n` for the stated literal and local-binding cases, but both examples have four entries and a three-character seal. Neither exercises a format-matching three-entry map. The “runtime-built” case also binds a literal rather than constructing the map through runtime operations.\n\nThe round 3 diff touches only the two stated files. Its hunks leave the accepted globals-lifecycle and kind-of changes, token-packet authentication, arity guard, witness admission, VM files, and `yang/core/call.cljc` unchanged; I found no call-node surgery, foreign `:code` extraction, or wrappers in that diff.\n\nOne landing qualification: locally, `git merge-base d3a35830 8fb525c4` is `7eb7fc9e`, so the reviewed head does not contain the landed master merge. The quoted checks are accepted as reported, but they do not by themselves establish the behavior of the eventual merge result. No dynamic checks were run in this review.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
